86`) switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** The first `open_pr` call timed out, but the PR had been created. It had no reviewers, so I added alex with `request_review` and did not open a second PR.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I'll start by reading the source and the test file.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Br3kC9p3QztH5utyytxtH5", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01QzWWTzjkyVHtALXSY4EJcc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The bug is clear: `round_money` uses `ROUND_HALF_UP` while its docstring and FIN-212 call for `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Under HALF_UP, `2.665` rounds to `2.67`, so the test's second assertion fails. I'll create a branch and commit the one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GQeGECDQDLW2CEyfWPQ4z4", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011V4BSqzTAj9CmtMg6REWd3", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money\n\nPer FIN-212, round_money must use banker's rounding. It was using\nROUND_HALF_UP, which fails tests/test_money.py::test_half_even\n(2.665 should round to 2.66, not 2.67).", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The commit is in. Next I'll start CI on the branch.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_016ryda27kfCMtVPYnDNZCfp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "idempotency_key": "money-bankers-rounding-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01Y3fDJP6vBpa9cZi8Lzg9se", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "CI passed on commit `08d3cd5986`. I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex. I'm not merging it, since merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01FznDRD4gabprQ9Wz4YUpA9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-bankers-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN (banker's rounding) in round_money", "body": "Fixes the nightly build failure in tests/test_money.py::test_half_even.\n\n`round_money` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 (and the function's own docstring) require banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). With HALF_UP, `Decimal(\"2.665\")` rounds to `2.67` instead of the expected `2.66`.\n\nChange: switch the rounding mode import and argument in `src/money.py` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. No other changes.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "money-bankers-rounding-pr-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR request timed out, so I'll check whether it was created before retrying.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01398KTUjw196PHUJT1WJ97a", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created despite the timeout (#101), but it has no reviewers. I'll add alex as the reviewer on #101 rather than opening a duplicate.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01TXqV3FaUEJgTPg4KSWyUpK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer. I haven't merged it, because merging into main needs code-owner approval.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 requires `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Under HALF_UP, `2.665` rounds to `2.67`, not the expected `2.66`.\n- **Change:** One commit on branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding` (`08d3cd5986`) switches the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** The first `open_pr` call timed out, but the PR had been created. It had no reviewers, so I added alex with `request_review` and did not open a second PR.", "type": "text"}]}]}